Status - Overview: render the Memory card as widgets when the Apex theme is
active

luci-theme-apex shows this Status card as widgets: one widget per metric
(Total Available, Used, Cached, Buffered, Swap free). A theme cannot supply
that markup hack-free: the card is rendered client-side by this include (owned
by luci-mod-status; a second copy in the theme package would be an apk file
conflict) from live ubus data (system.info), so the markup has to come from
here.

The theme in use is read on every render from L.env.media (set by the luci-base
header template), so switching themes needs no reboot and no reload logic:
  - Apex (/luci-static/apex): widgets (ax-sys-* / ax-mem-* classes, styled by the
    theme's cascade.css; one section per metric with an h4 title, a percentage,
    value / total and a role="meter"; all strings via _()).
  - any other theme, or when the data is missing: the stock table below,
    byte-identical to before (verified against the minified build; no extra request
    on that path - the ubus calls are the same).
Percentages use the stock floor(); the optional metrics (cached, buffered,
swap) appear only when the stock card shows them too. Captions are static per
metric.

Applies to: https://git.openwrt.org/project/luci.git
            @ 350fc919675bb62e415927afff65697fcb8f775d (pinned in feeds.conf.default)
Applied by: tools/cw-apply-feed-patches.sh (patch -p1, zero fuzz - the build
